OPERATOR DECISION (2026-08-07): the direct-Anthropic arm IS approved as a fallback.

This answers the ticket's own open question. The fallback is INTENDED to be configured and reachable in normal local/CI operation — it is not deliberately unreachable outside the provider matrix. Therefore the 401 is a REAL defect, not an artifact of an intentionally-blanked key.

Consequences for the fix:
- the arm must be genuinely functional: a valid ANTHROPIC_API_KEY must be resolvable in normal operation, so a Bedrock rejection actually falls back rather than failing twice;
- rebar.toml's note that the Bedrock arm 'deliberately blanks ANTHROPIC_API_KEY' applies to the PROVIDER MATRIX only, and the config/docs should say so explicitly so this is not re-litigated;
- a test should prove the fallback path is exercised end-to-end, not merely attempted — the current failure mode (attempt, 401, misleading error) would still pass a test that only asserts 'fallback was tried'.
